WEBVTT

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.590
Let's go and don't cry, funny

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.520
Give me a dumbass dream, please

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.760
Don't touch me, baby

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.960
Freedom, baby

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.870
I'm elastic, I want to be chained

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:43.470
Can you feel it? The nonsensical afterimage

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:55.220
Even the moments of points and lines
disappear after failing to show

00:00:55.220 --> 00:01:00.960
The sad forefront, an empty sensation

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.630
Sweet remnants that tear at my heart

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:12.300
Scattering Polaroids, gathering paranoia

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.470
I want you to tell me whose turn is next

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:30.840
If you sleep close to this incomplete
form, you'll understand and see

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.020
We'll start passing things out now!

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.160
- Bread!
- Stew!

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.130
Is there anyone who feels ill or who is injured?

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:48.470
Please raise your hand! I'll come to you!

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.110
Be careful! It's hot!

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.490
Here, have a lot!

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:08.680
- Are you sure?!
- Thanks!

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.450
Okay, say, "Ah!"

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.190
Does anyone not have bread yet?

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.570
All you outsiders can disappear together!

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.400
Burn up, all of you!

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.840
Stay low to the ground!
Don't breathe in the smoke!

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:27.500
Zaza!

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.410
It's the end!

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.980
It's the end! The day of judgment!

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.610
This way, everyone!

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.000
That way! Hurry!

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.400
Look out!

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.070
Xargin!

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.110
I've fixed your glasses.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.120
The people in the church...

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.460
Are they all right?

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.730
Yeah, they're all fine.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:22.130
They moved to some
abandoned apartments in Ward 14.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.890
That's a relief...

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:29.640
You're a native citizen...
Why are you helping immigrants?

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.770
Why would I ignore people who are suffering?

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:38.480
Citizens and immigrants are the
same human beings God created.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.820
How could anyone ignore
others who are suffering?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.950
The same human beings...

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.450
Xargin! They said you were hurt!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.590
I'm fine. It's nothing much.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:51.090
Wait!

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:54.360
Sasha. He's a new friend of mine.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.830
Huh? Um...

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.930
It's nice to meet you. I'm Sasha.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.540
Oh, it's nice to meet you, too. I'm...

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.280
This rosary...

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:13.370
Oh, this is the one and only
thing I have from when I was a baby...

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:16.520
Are you Joseph?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.680
How do you know my name?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.260
- You are Joseph, aren't you?
- Who are you?

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:28.750
Your sister, Joseph! I'm your older sister!

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.460
Oh, thank you, God!

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.540
The priest raised you?

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:46.310
Yeah. He raised me and
taught me many important things.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:50.750
Sasha.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:54.590
How did you and Joseph end up separated?

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:59.260
I was entered into service
shortly after Joseph was born.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:02.360
Entering into service meant I'd be fed.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.430
They said it was better than staying
and plummeting into ruin with them.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.140
I had no idea at all...

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:14.010
Our father made that
rosary to celebrate your birth.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:17.650
And I was able to meet you now thanks to it.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:21.380
It's almost like a dream,
being able to live together again!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.870
What do you do now, Sister?

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.290
So this is a university...

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:31.690
Sasha specializes in bioengineering.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.800
She does nanomachine research in her lab.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.600
If her research works out,
people will no longer die from disease.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.040
Huh?!

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:45.710
Sasha is trying to dramatically
evolve people in a good direction.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:48.940
Almost like a miracle of God!

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.080
A miracle of God...

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.050
And once that happens, Joseph...

00:05:54.050 --> 00:06:00.290
Never again will children too poor
to buy medicine perish from disease!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:03.260
Amazing! That's amazing, Sister!

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:10.400
There's no one on or near the
campus who doesn't know about Sasha!

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.740
That's because I'm the first
outsider to ever be a researcher.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.840
I seem strange to everyone, that's all.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:21.080
Joseph! Sasha studied and worked
at the same time and got a scholarship!

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.710
That's double-amazing!

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.550
Then what about you, Xargin?

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:29.950
I'm a medical school intern and the
organ player at this school's church.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.190
When she's not doing research,

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:35.290
Sasha helps with my immigrant support work.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.690
Xargin!

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.360
She's a little better than you!

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.900
Quiet, you!

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.230
Quit it!

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.300
I'll teach ya to talk insolently to me!

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.890
It was just a joke!

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.430
- Lt's a university truck!
- A university truck! Joseph!

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:55.540
Thanks!

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.980
Sleep warmly, everyone!

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:01.450
Is your injury all better, Xargin?

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:04.720
I don't think that would've
been categorized as an injury.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:07.120
See! I'm A-OK!

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.760
I'll help out, too!

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.630
Oh! How dependable!

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:16.560
All the adults are out doing
work to clean up after the flood.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.170
So you're all by yourselves today?

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:22.660
Everyone's so happy to have found work!

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:31.510
The day of judgment is coming.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:35.000
The judgment of the apocalypse is coming...

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:40.860
The attack on the church drove her crazy...

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.820
Umm... Please use this.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.000
The time of judgment is coming!

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.660
Zaza!

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:52.700
What's wrong, Lulu?!

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.860
It's Annika! She needs help!

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.940
- She has a terrible fever!
- Let's get her to the hospital!

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:08.880
Sasha! Hospitals won't treat
immigrant children without identification!

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.750
Joseph! Get my medical bag from the truck!

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:12.850
Right!

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.290
- Zaza! Where do you live?!
- This way!

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.830
Xargin! Your bag!

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.320
Boil some water!

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.670
Zaza. Step outside.

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:35.400
- But...
- Just go!

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.240
Please let us be in time...

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:54.430
What's wrong? Isn't
Annika over the worst of it now?

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.920
Annika has scarlet fever.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:02.440
- Lt's an infectious children's disease.
- Infectious?!

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.040
It has an incubation period of two to four days.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:09.440
There's a high probability it
spread among everyone in the church.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:15.480
Antibiotics can cure it, but
it's fatal if it isn't treated in time.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:20.250
As you can see, there are
hardly any antibiotics in my bag.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:24.730
We would need enormous
funds to get as much as we need.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.200
But none of us have that kind of money...

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.600
Then...

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:33.270
Worst case scenario, in the next few
days it spreads to not just this block,

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:36.840
but to all the neighboring
blocks with poor immigrants!

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:44.050
And if that happens,
countless children will lose their lives!

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:45.150
Xargin!

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.850
Zaza. You'll need to stay
somewhere else tonight...

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.780
Lulu and Nelly are burning up too...

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.520
"Medical supply room"...This is it.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.570
What are you doing here, Xargin?!

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:09.540
We're probably here for the same thing.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:14.310
I'm fine! But you'll never get
to be a doctor if you get caught!

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:18.010
What kind of doctor
would stand to let children die?

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.070
You idiot...!

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.820
The supply room!

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:30.160
Uh oh! They're coming!

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:33.650
Hurry! Come on!

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:37.590
Hurry!

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:47.570
Wh-What's with these soldiers?!

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:53.480
Place the stolen items on the ground!

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:56.250
They didn't steal anything!

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:59.690
The director gave that medicine to me!

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:02.620
Isn't that right, Director Victor?

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:07.190
I've surely done enough
research to warrant such a reward.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:15.390
Do these two know what
your research is being used for?

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.910
All right. But only this once.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:27.250
Sasha. What's going on?

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:28.310
Let's hurry.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:38.930
Administer this right
away if any symptoms appear.

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:40.900
Just take the cap off and inject it.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:45.200
Tell as many people as you can!

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.700
Is that really a good idea?

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:50.470
That's just gonna increase
the number of outsiders, Doc.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:53.240
Why would a doctor wanna make more garbage?

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.770
Don't listen to them.
Someday they'll understand too.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.720
- Are you all better now, Annika?
- Yeah!

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:06.650
Really? That's good to hear!

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:08.460
Mom!

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:11.560
I'm okay. Just a little dizzy, that's all.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:15.230
You've hardly eaten anything lately, Mom.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.260
You always let us have your food...

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:19.600
It's okay. I'm a grownup.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:22.660
Well, it's time for me to go to work...

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:26.810
Really! It's nothing!

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.970
Then what was with those
military-like security guards?!

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:34.310
What did the director use your research for?!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:41.060
Won't you tell me what's bothering you, Sasha?

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:46.990
My research was meant to save
children who can't buy medicine.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:51.100
But... they're using it
for something horrifying...

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:52.760
Horrifying?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.600
I'm sorry!

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.100
Sasha!

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.670
They aren't being paid?!

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:03.980
Nope. They're not gonna pay Mom
and the others for their chore work

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:06.680
until all the flood cleanup work is finished.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.220
That's so mean...

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:13.950
I think they're bringing us
back all the food they get for lunch.

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:18.410
They look pale, too. What happens if Mom dies?

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:20.800
Zaza?

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.330
I've decided.

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.350
Decided what?

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:32.370
Sasha? I haven't seen her since she
went into town early this afternoon.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.030
Thanks.

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:38.200
Where did you go, Sasha?

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:53.430
Lousy immigrant, tryin' to
be some fancy researcher...

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:57.770
You must be trickin' that young
doc into doing all kinds of stuff!

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.100
You outsider witch!

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.070
Execute the witch!

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:07.670
If you want to strike me down, then do it!

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.210
Sasha!

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:14.880
Sister!

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.680
Sasha!

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:22.490
Xargin...

00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:30.230
Why?! Why not me, instead of you?!

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:32.300
Because she's an outsider!

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:36.240
Violence is always directed at the weak.

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:41.140
It's directed at helpless people
who are easy to beat, easy to kill.

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:43.410
That's how violence works!

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:49.350
Sasha... I'm...

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:49.950
Lulu!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.850
She was at the gate,
shouting your names and crying...

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:56.690
Everyone's going to die...

00:14:56.690 --> 00:15:02.230
Zaza collapsed, and so did
Sepp and Ema and everyone else!

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:06.300
They have really bad fevers!
They're all going to die!

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:11.510
Are there not enough adults
to administer the medicine?!

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.670
Go...

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.340
Sasha!

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:18.980
Both of you... go...

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:23.440
Save... the children...

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:37.090
Lulu...

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:42.970
It'll be all right. I'm sure
Xargin will save them all.

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:51.210
The medicine is gone?!

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:54.480
When I came home, I couldn't
find Zaza's medicine anywhere!

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.780
Please help him! Help Zaza!

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:58.450
Zaza!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:02.090
Zaza! Where's your medicine?!

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:04.590
I'm sorry...

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:10.000
I'm sorry... I sold the medicine for money...

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.700
You sold your medicine?!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.190
That bread! Don't tell me you!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:18.070
Zaza! That bread you got from a truck!

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:20.940
Don't tell me you sold the medicine to buy it!

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:24.650
I really wanted... you to have bread...

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:28.120
Don't speak, Zaza. Breathe.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:34.120
I'm sorry... I'm...

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:35.780
Zaza...

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:28.480
Yes. Everything is wrong with this world.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:34.280
An irrational, hideous world in which
the innocent are always trampled on.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:38.190
The world must be righted, in God's name.

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:46.750
Xargin. In mind and body, you are
worthy of carrying out this noble act.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.300
This is from Sasha.

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:54.290
She said to give it to you
should anything happen to her.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:18:00.140
From the moment she became
the first outsider to be a researcher

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:03.770
she seemed prepared
to die in a manner like this.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:13.880
Joseph. I'm afraid I wasn't
worthy of the respect you had for me.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:18.790
My research intended to save children

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:22.020
wound up being used for a horrifying purpose.

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:30.800
It produced technology capable of
changing people into living weapons

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.540
by combining their blood with nanomachines.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.200
Living weapons?!

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:48.590
Are you insane, Xargin?!

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:53.760
Have you forgotten your mission
of righting the world in God's name?!

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:56.960
You are in no position to mention God's name.

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:01.060
All you people want is to rule this world.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:04.830
Stop, Xargin!

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:13.310
Save the children...

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:16.350
What did Sasha die for?

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:20.220
Why did those children have to die?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:26.990
How many more children must be
born and die until the world changes?!

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:32.800
I finally realize what that hag
meant when she spoke of the apocalypse.

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:35.800
I must end this suffering.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:38.140
I am going to end this world!

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:39.800
Xargin!

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:43.970
Stop!

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:01.860
Xargin...

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:05.130
Life is worth living.

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:11.040
No matter how cruel the
world may be, life is worth living...

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:15.280
You can't take that away.

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:19.210
In that case, you can live in suffering.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:31.590
When I woke, my body had changed.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.400
Use this to go after Xargin.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:39.390
Or else he'll destroy all of humankind.

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:10.090
Mei-Fong?!

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:20.170
Sasha?!

00:21:54.170 --> 00:22:05.290
I dreamed of that day we chased shooting stars

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:15.700
What we had kept safe disappeared like sand

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:19.770
Just another illusion

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:28.870
Asleep, inside memories

00:22:30.110 --> 00:22:32.410
Wish for the stars

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:40.950
Holding countless wishes with both hands

00:22:40.950 --> 00:22:43.520
A wish for the stars

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:51.470
Quietly by your side, as you sleep

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:57.100
Yes, right next to you

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:03.080
Holding countless wishes

00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:08.840
Yes, right beside you

00:23:13.190 --> 00:23:16.660
Amid turmoil, the world changes.

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:21.860
Holy light illuminates a
previously concealed plan.

00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:26.730
Episode 15: "The Millenary Knights of God."

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:31.600
From the dark reaches of
history an ancient ambition is revived.
